{"trial": "t03", "round": 1, "status": "ok", "dev_success": 0.8398, "train_success_last10pct": 0.7695, "wall_s": 159.7, "params": 84870, "config": {"lr": 0.0007, "lr_schedule": "linear_decay", "n_envs": 256, "rollout_len": 16, "ppo_epochs": 2, "n_minibatches": 4, "gamma": 0.95, "gae_lambda": 0.9, "clip_eps": 0.2, "ent_coef": 0.01, "vf_coef": 0.5, "max_grad_norm": 1.0, "adv_norm": true, "encoder": "conv", "width": 64, "depth": 3, "activation": "relu", "norm": "none", "obs_mode": "heightmaps", "reward_mode": "heightmap_delta", "success_bonus": 1.0, "step_penalty": 0.0}, "your_hypothesis": "Heightmap observations with a deeper conv net and heightmap_delta reward give a compact input matching the target structure, which may speed learning. If overhang information matters and success falls below baseline, voxels are needed."}
